00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:24.620
us remotely.

00:01:25.019 --> 00:01:28.819
Um, you may notice that our numbers are down a bit tonight.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.779
We, uh, Ms Mayor Battle and council member David Little,

00:01:32.849 --> 00:01:37.059
they are both out of town and we look forward to having them rejoin us at

00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:41.739
our next meeting, uh, but be assured a quorum of the council is present

00:01:41.739 --> 00:01:43.620
and we will conduct our business tonight.

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:48.430
We will begin by an invocation offered by one of our Huntsville,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.750
Alabama public safety chaplains, chaplain Scott Lowry.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.970
He will be followed by Pledge of Allegiance,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.669
uh, which we led by council member Bill Kling.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.629
All who wish to stand for the invocation and pledge,

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.500
please do so.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:11.199
It's been a privilege to serve this my 20th year as a volunteer police chaplain.

00:02:11.529 --> 00:02:12.889
We've seen a lot happen.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:18.610
I stood beside Mayor Battle in the hallway of UAH when there were no words

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.630
to speak 16 years ago.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:24.050
We've seen God bless this community tremendously.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.050
May we never take those blessings for granted.

00:02:27.839 --> 00:02:28.520
Let's pray.

00:02:29.699 --> 00:02:33.539
Father, we come before you with thanksgiving.

00:02:34.259 --> 00:02:38.660
I thank you for the privilege of living and ministering in a progressive

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.619
community but also a community with um.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.100
Moral value.

00:02:45.509 --> 00:02:49.580
I pray God that you will give our leaders continued wisdom,

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.830
help us never to take the blessing of living where we live for granted,

00:02:55.119 --> 00:02:58.149
but to understand that you've been very, very good to us.

00:02:58.479 --> 00:03:03.509
We pray, Lord, for our leadership tonight for the things that will be discussed.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.690
We pray for our state we pray for our country.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.350
And we ask for your blessings we ask for wisdom and once again thank you

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.059
for the way you've poured your blessings out throughout the years.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.940
Bless now in all that is said and all that is done,

00:03:18.059 --> 00:03:19.630
and we will give you the praise.

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:20.259
Amen.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.699
For which it stands, one nation under God,

00:03:35.119 --> 00:03:38.089
indivisible, with liberty and justice for all.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.210
Thank you so much for your 20 years of service,

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.350
Chaplain Lowery.

00:03:46.509 --> 00:03:47.740
