00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:11.600
Uh, Buffalo Soldiers, American Legion Post 351 for over 60 years of service

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.809
to the Huntsville community, is there a motion to approve motion from Ms.

00:06:14.899 --> 00:06:15.380
Watkins.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.179
Second from Mr.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:16.500
Kling.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.299
All in favor, please.

00:06:17.529 --> 00:06:19.179
And Kate, I opposed motion carries.

00:06:19.299 --> 00:06:19.380
Ms.

00:06:19.459 --> 00:06:21.279
Watkins, would you like to make that presentation?

00:06:25.179 --> 00:06:26.420
Oh, sorry, microphone.

00:06:27.619 --> 00:06:27.649
There you go.

00:06:38.209 --> 00:06:38.989
Good evening.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.040
Can I have the 10th cavalry soldiers please come up,

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:42.790
please.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.420
So while they're coming up, let me tell you all a little background about

00:06:58.420 --> 00:06:58.549
myself.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:02.649
Come on up on the stage, um, before I read the resolution,

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:09.040
I grew up and went to school in elementary at Calvert Hills Elementary School,

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.100
and throughout the time that I was at Caver Hills,

00:07:12.149 --> 00:07:14.290
this is why your history is so important,

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.529
and I talked to several people that went to school with me because I thought,

00:07:17.989 --> 00:07:19.190
how did I miss that?

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.869
But no one never told us why the school was named Caver Hill.

00:07:24.299 --> 00:07:28.820
And throughout the years when we came to learn why it was called Calvary

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:33.339
Hills, and a lot of people refer to it as 10th Cavalry instead of Calvary

00:07:33.339 --> 00:07:37.619
Hills, and it's so important for us to teach our history,

00:07:37.739 --> 00:07:39.739
know our history, and recognize our history.

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:40.144
History.

00:07:40.225 --> 00:07:44.744
So that's why tonight I have them here because I wanna recognize them for

00:07:44.744 --> 00:07:46.545
the hard work that they do in the community.

00:07:46.704 --> 00:07:50.204
So I'm gonna read some of the resolution and then I'm gonna turn it over

00:07:50.204 --> 00:07:50.785
to Mr.

00:07:50.825 --> 00:07:51.385
Walker.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:53.904
Are you, you Sergeant Major, right?

00:07:54.744 --> 00:07:55.464
First Sergeant.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:04.320
OK, whereas the city council and mayor of Huntsville recognized the 10th

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:10.160
Cavalry Hills Buffalo Soldier American Legion Post 351 as a distinguished

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:15.100
veterans organization whose members have faithfully served both our nation

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.799
and the Huntsville community through military service,

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.540
civic leadership, and unwavering commitment to equality and service.

00:08:22.904 --> 00:08:25.755
Whereas following honorable military service,

00:08:26.065 --> 00:08:30.625
nearly 300 veterans from Huntsville, Madison County and surrounding communities

00:08:30.625 --> 00:08:36.065
united to established American Legion Post 351 after being denied equal

00:08:36.065 --> 00:08:38.815
access to existing American Legion facilities,

00:08:39.065 --> 00:08:44.844
receiving their official charter in 1961 following years of perseverance

00:08:44.844 --> 00:08:45.645
and determination.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:51.809
Whereas the founding members of Post 351 car for the proud legacy of generations

00:08:51.809 --> 00:08:54.229
of African American servicemen and women,

00:08:55.049 --> 00:08:57.809
including the Buffalo Soldier, the Tuskegee Airmen,

00:08:57.969 --> 00:09:03.559
the 369th Infantry Regiment, and the 761 Tank Battalion,

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:07.330
and countless others who answered the call to defend our nation with courage

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.210
and distinction.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:13.469
Whereas throughout its history, Post 351 has demonstrated remarkable resilience

00:09:13.669 --> 00:09:18.150
by overcoming numerous challenges, preserving its charter through the dedication

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.950
of generations of commanders, officers, members,

00:09:20.989 --> 00:09:25.669
and volunteers who remain steadfast in their commitment to serving veterans

00:09:25.669 --> 00:09:30.359
in the community, whereas the Post has made lasting contributions to Huntsville

00:09:30.359 --> 00:09:31.630
through youth mentorship.

00:09:31.815 --> 00:09:35.585
Educational program, boy state sponsorship,

00:09:35.786 --> 00:09:38.505
oratorical competitions, tutoring initiatives,

00:09:38.906 --> 00:09:43.026
community service projects, and advocacy on behalf of veterans and their

00:09:43.026 --> 00:09:45.666
families while promoting the principles of duty,

00:09:45.945 --> 00:09:51.705
honor, patriotism, and citizenship, whereas in 2024 the members voted to

00:09:51.705 --> 00:09:54.726
rename the organization the 10th Cavalry.

00:09:55.101 --> 00:10:00.541
Buffalo Soldiers, American Legion Post 351 in recognition of the historic

00:10:00.541 --> 00:10:04.942
legacy of the Buffalo Soldiers who once camped in North Huntsville and to

00:10:04.942 --> 00:10:08.781
honor the enduring connection between the legacy and the service of the

00:10:08.781 --> 00:10:09.651
Post members.

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:14.812
For more than 6 decades, the members of Post 351 has strengthened the Huntsville

00:10:14.812 --> 00:10:17.002
community through their dedication of veterans,

00:10:17.341 --> 00:10:17.882
youth.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:24.590
Education, public service, and preservation of African American military

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:29.229
history inspiring future generations through their enduring example of leadership

00:10:29.229 --> 00:10:29.989
and perseverance.

00:10:30.119 --> 00:10:33.710
Now let it therefore be resolved that the city council and the mayor of

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:35.849
Huntsville, Alabama do hereby congratulate.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:38.969
And honors 10th Cavalry Hill Buffalo Soldiers,

00:10:39.419 --> 00:10:44.460
American Legion Post 351 upon its continued legacy of service and expressed

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:49.109
sincere appreciation for more than 60 years of dedicated commitment to veterans,

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:53.760
youth, community service, and preservation of the proud military heritage

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:58.000
and history of African Americans in Huntsville and the state of Alabama

00:10:58.049 --> 00:10:58.820
and our nation.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:00.500
Can Hannah.

00:11:05.669 --> 00:11:08.179
Thank you, uh, Councilwoman Watkins.

00:11:08.229 --> 00:11:11.890
Uh, normally first I do a lot of talk, but tonight we're not gonna do this.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:14.869
So I wanted to say happy birthday to America,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.119
250 years of perseverance, and I wanna thank the mayor,

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.219
Councilwoman Watkins, the city council members,

00:11:22.469 --> 00:11:26.090
and all of you for coming, and we appreciate this award and this recognition,

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.669
and we will carry forward from this day forward.

00:11:28.869 --> 00:11:29.520
Thank you.

00:11:29.859 --> 00:11:30.570
Thank you.

00:12:10.059 --> 00:12:12.599
Thank you all for 60 years of service.

